:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:35.665826+00:00","sthala_purana":"One of the Shakti Peethas — by most accounts marking where the third eye or the eyeball of Sati fell — and one of the major seats of Tantric practice in Bengal. Tradition holds that the sage Vashishtha attained siddhi (spiritual accomplishment) here through Tantric sadhana, and the temple remains closely associated with the adjoining cremation ground on the Dwarka riverbank.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"তারাপীঠ মন্দির","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Kazi Nazrul Islam Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":76.1,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Mallarpur railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":7,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":null,"architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"b2928600-0b0b-43eb-8e1b-58e8f9d8a499","name":"Parshuram Mahadev Temple","deity":"Shiva as Mahadev","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Rajasthan","district":"Rajsamand","town":"Bardara","latitude":25.13917,"longitude":73.5325,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Magai River","river_distance_km":6.2,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:03:56.940052+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A cave Shiva temple in the Aravalli foothills on the Rajsamand-Pali border, about 10 km from Kumbhalgarh. Reached by around 500 steps from the Sadri side. According to tradition, Parshuram carved the cave with his axe and worshipped Shiva here. It has natural forms of Shiva and Ganesha and nine kunds said ne