"Shaiva","significance":["Arupadaiveedu"],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Tiruvallur","town":"Tiruttani","latitude":13.17183,"longitude":79.60377,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Kusasthalaiyar","river_distance_km":8,"best_season_notes":"Oct–Feb; the 365 steps to the hilltop shrine are best climbed before the heat of the day.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-05T11:47:46.109676+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:35.665826+00:00","sthala_purana":"One of the six Arupadaiveedu (sacred abodes of Murugan), set atop a hill 700 feet above the surrounding plain and reached by 365 steps, one for each day of the year. Tradition holds Murugan rested here to compose himself after slaying the demon Surapadman. It is also here that Indra gave his daughter Deivayanai in marriage to Murugan, along with his white elephant Airavata as dowry; Murugan offered to return the elephant, but Indra asked only that it face his direction, and the temple's elephant image still faces east as a result. The temple is celebrated in the Sangam-era Tirumurugatrupadai of Nakkeerar, with later patronage from the Vijayanagara empire and local chieftains.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"திருத்தணி முருகன் கோயில்","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Tirupati Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":51.7,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Tiruttani railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":1.2,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Sangam-era Tirumurugatrupadai; local/regional tradition","architecture_style":"Dravidian (Vijayanagara-era patronage)","construction_century":null},{"id":"b4bce6b7-2d04-4d67-b797-8bf4587c90e8","name":"Ragigudda Anjaneya Temple","deity":"Hanuman as Prasanna Anjaneyaswamy","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Karnataka","district":"Bengaluru Urban","town":"Bengaluru","latitude":12.91424,"longitude":77.5932,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Vrishabavathi River","river_distance_km":7,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:11.054915+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Hanuman temple on a hillock in Jayanagar, Bengaluru, covering about 5 acres. The precinct also houses a Shivalinga, shrines to Rama, Sita and Lakshmana, and a Trimurti shrine on carved rocks. Smaller temples to Ganesha, the Navagrahas and Rajarajeshwari stand at the base. The Ragigudda metro station is a few hundred metres away.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Kempegowda International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":33.8,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Krantivira Sangolli Rayanna (Bengaluru) railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":7.6,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Ragigudda Anjaneya Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"b4e09782-3a2f-4156-9f20-78101e537f8d","name":"Shri Sai Baba Temple, Shirdi","deity":"Sai Baba of Shirdi","sampradaya":null,"significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Maharashtra","district":"Ahilyanagar","town":"Savalivihir Budruk","latitude":19.76618,"longitude":74.477,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Godavari River","river_distance_km":9.4,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:38:38.196668+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Also called the Samadhi Mandir, this large temple complex at Shirdi in Ahilyanagar district, Maharashtra, honours the 19th-century saint Sai Baba of Shirdi. It is one of the most visited pilgrimage sites in India, drawing millions of devotees each year from India and abroad.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Shirdi Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":13.7,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Sainagar Shirdi railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":1.6,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Shri Sai Baba Temple, Shirdi), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"b619b710-e6b1-4300-9e88-dae83229c2bf","name":"Agneeswarar Temple, Kanjanur","deity":"Agneeswarar (Shiva) / Karpagambal","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":["Navagraha Sthalam"],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Thanjavur","town":"Kanjanur","latitude":11.06583,"longitude":79.4625,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Cauvery delta","river_distance_km":3,"best_season_notes":"Oct–Feb; Fridays, associated with Sukra, are considered auspicious.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-05T11:47:03.785954+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:35.665826+00:00","sthala_purana":"The Navagraha Sthalam for Sukra (Venus), who — in keeping with the Saiva belief that Shiva is omnipresent — is held to reside within the presiding deity's own form. The 7th-century Nayanar saint Thirunavukkarasar sang ten verses in praise of this shrine in the Tevaram, naming the goddess here Karpagambal. The temple traces to the Chola period, with major renovation under the Vijayanagara empire.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"அக்னீஸ்வரர் கோயில், கஞ்சனூர்","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Thanjavur Air Force Station","nearest_airport_distance_km":54.1,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Aduturai railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":6.5,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Tevaram canon; local/regional tradition","architecture_style":"Dravidian (Chola, Vijayanagara)","construction_century":null},{"id":"b63ab5a7-7b9c-4424-9a7f-dee4db70ba1c","name":"Trinetreshwar Temple","deity":"Shiva as Trinetreshwar","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Gujarat","district":"Surendranagar","town":"Thangadh Taluka","latitude":22.64583,"longitude":71.21333,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":null,"river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:38:36.086063+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:35.665826+00:00","sthala_purana":"Trinetreshwar Temple is a Shiva temple in Pratihara style at Tarnetar village in Surendra