 temples near the Chambal river, in Pratihara style. It is around 50 km from Kota and is protected by the Archaeological Survey of India.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Kota Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":33.9,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Alniya railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":32.8,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Ghateshwar Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Pratihara","construction_century":null},{"id":"b84a2cb4-357e-4cbc-9531-415940e9f80e","name":"Kanchi Kamakoti Peetham","deity":"Chandramouleeswara / Kamakshi","sampradaya":"Smartha","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Kanchipuram","town":"Kanchipuram","latitude":12.8397,"longitude":79.705,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"pure_veg_available","food_source_name":"Kanchi Mutt Nitya Annadanam (free lunch)","food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Vegavathy","river_distance_km":1,"best_season_notes":"Dec–Mar. Walkable from both the Kamakshi Amman and Ekambareswarar temples; the same northeast-monsoon timing (heaviest rain Oct–Nov) applies across Kanchipuram.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-03T13:44:40.752775+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:00.624755+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Smartha matha at Kanchipuram, held by its own tradition to have been established by Adi Shankaracharya as a fifth seat, though it is not counted among the four Amnaya peethams in every account. It has long been a centre of Sri Vidya upasana and Vedic scholarship in the Tamil country.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"காஞ்சி காமகோடி பீடம்","