i","town":"West Mambalam","latitude":13.0375,"longitude":80.2205,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Adyar River","river_distance_km":1.7,"best_season_notes":"Nov–Feb.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-08T06:51:40.218447+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Built in 1978, a shrine to the fierce village-guardian form of Devi worshipped widely across Tamil Nadu as Angala Parameswari, roughly 10 minutes from Vani Mahal.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Chennai International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":7.6,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Mambalam railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":0.8,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Contributor-submitted local survey","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":20},{"id":"bd41845d-a215-4264-932a-4b40d64f33d4","name":"Thirumeninathar temple","deity":"Shiva as Thirumeninathar","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Sivagangai","town":"Dhayapuram","latitude":9.7,"longitude":78.483,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Vaigai River","river_distance_km":3.1,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:14.599574+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Shiva temple at Tiruchuli, a Paadal Petra Sthalam praised in the Tevaram and linked to the saint Sundarar. Shiva is worshipped as a lingam, with Parvati as Thunaimalaiyammai Amman. Tradition says many gods and sages worshipped here, and Ramana Maharishi was born in Tiruchuli.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Madurai International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":45.7,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Manamadurai Junction railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":3.7,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Thirumeninathar temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"bd7b6fdd-7b59-4c88-a241-634ec1ef8fe9","name":"ISKCON Temple, Patna","deity":"Radha Banke Bihari","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Bihar","district":"Patna","town":"Danapur","latitude":25.60806,"longitude":85.13444,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Ganges River","river_distance_km":3.2,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:59.639499+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"The Sri Sri Radha Banke Bihari Temple of ISKCON on Budh Marg in Patna, the first ISKCON temple in Bihar and the largest in the city by campus area. The complex was developed in phases between 2010 and 2023, with the temple inaugurated on 3 May 2022. It hosts Patna's yearly Jagannath Ratha Yatra and other Vaishnava festivals.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Jayprakash Narayan International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":5,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Patna Junction railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":0.6,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (ISKCON Temple, Patna), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":21},{"id":"bdc3df87-ea94-42e9-8504-aedb898f6fb0","name":"Jambukeswarar Temple, Tiruvanaikaval (Appu Sthalam)","deity":"Shiva (Jambukeswarar)","sampradaya":null,"significance":["Pancha Bhoota Sthalam"],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Tiruchirappalli","town":"Tiruvanaikaval","latitude":10.8531,"longitude":78.7047,"sandhya_friendly":"yes","sandhya_notes":"The Kaveri flows close to this island-adjacent temple town.","samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Kaveri","river_distance_km":0.8,"best_season_notes":"Dec–Mar; pairs naturally with Srirangam's Ranganathaswamy Temple nearby. Tiruchirappalli sits in the same northeast-monsoon belt as the rest of Tamil Nadu, with its wettest weeks typically in Oct–Nov.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-03T11:51:56.898831+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:00.624755+00:00","sthala_purana":"Tradition holds that Shiva took the form of a bull and remained at the foot of this hill, and that the temple was raised at the site by the Chalukya king. The Kaveri encircles the shrine, and the sanctum is kept perpetually damp by a spring — which is why it is counted as the water element among the Pancha Bhoota Sthalams.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"ஜம்புகேஸ்வரர் கோயில்","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Tiruchirapalli International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":10.1,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Srirangam railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":1.1,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":null,"architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"bdee7b5d-4add-42d3-90f6-b37e237309ab","name":"Beeramgunta Poleramma Temple","deity":"Poleramma","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Andhra Pradesh","district":"Sri Potti Sriramulu Nellore","town":"Beeramgunta","latitude":14.62814,"longitude":80.03513,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Penna River","river_distance_km":10.8,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:05:20.030396+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A re-established temple in Nellore district, Andhra Pradesh, said to be about 200 years old. Poleramma is a village guardian goddess and a local form of Shakti. Unlike most such shrines, which lie on village outskirts, this one was set in the centre of the village.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Tirupati Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":122.8,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Talamanchi railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":4.7,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Beeramgunta Poleramma Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"be55aa17-4f19-4b32-9256-bb0d043da23d","name":"Erakeswara Temple, Pillalamarri","deity":"Shiva as Erakeswara","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Telangana","district":"Suryapet","town":"Pillalamarri","latitude":17.16968,"longitude":79.5822,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Musi","river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:11.054915+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:00.624755+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Shaiva temple on the Musi river bank in Pillalamarri, built around 1208 CE and commissioned by Erakasani, wife of Beti Reddi of the Recherla Reddis, feudatories of the Kakatiyas. It is one of four richly carved stone temples at the village, the others being Nameswara, Trikuteswara and Chennakesava.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Warangal Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":82.8,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Tipparthi railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":24.8,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Erakeswara Temple, Pillalamarri), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Kakatiya-era carved stone","construction_century":13},{"id":"bee22966-a511-44f6-a97d-b36085d5a240","name":"Bhadrakali Temple, Kurukshetra","deity":"Bhadrakali","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":["Shakti Peetha"],"country":"India","state":"Haryana","district":"Kurukshetra","town":"Kurukshetra","latitude":29.9695,"longitude":76.8783,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":null,"river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":"Oct–Mar. Often visited alongside Brahma Sarovar and Jyotisar in the same town.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-03T20:39:31.59741+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:00.624755+00:00","sthala_purana":"Held by tradition to be one of the Shakti Peethas, marking the spot where an anklet (or the ankle) of Sati fell. Kurukshetra's association with the Mahabharata war makes this one of the temples the Pandavas are said to have worshipped at before battle.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"भद्रकाली मन्दिर","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Sarsawa Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":50.9,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Kurukshetra Junction railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":2.6,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Devi Bhagavata Purana / Shakti Peetha tradition (Sati-limb legend)","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"bf497bee-ea98-4141-9dd0-e8561caa66a1","name":"Varadharajaperumal temple, Thirubuvanai","deity":"Vishnu as Varadaraja Perumal","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Puducherry","district":"Puducherry","town":"Thirubuvanai","latitude":11.9275,"longitude":79.6475,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Chenjiyaru River","river_distance_km":6.4,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:03:52.882408+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Vishnu temple at Thirubuvanai village near Puducherry, in Dravidian style and believed to have been built by Parantaka I. Inscriptions from Rajaraja Chola's time record an educational institution here. A granite wall encloses the shrines, the gateway tower is flat, worship follows the Vaikhanasa tradition, and the ASI maintains it.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Puducherry Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":18.5,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Chinnababu Samudram railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":4.4,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Varadharajaperumal temple, Thirubuvanai), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Dravidian (Chola)","construction_century":10},{"id":"bfeb555d-061c-459a-83a0-a2dd6ca578cf","name":"Moti Dungri","deity":"Ganesha","sampradaya":"Ganapatya","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Rajasthan","district":"Jaipur","town":"Jaipur","latitude":26.89462,"longitude":75.81674,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Amanisha River","river_distance_km":5.3,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:38:01.041713+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Ganesha temple complex in Jaipur, Rajasthan, built in 1761 under the supervision of Seth Jai Ram Paliwal. It is a popular visitor attraction and stands beside the Birla Temple.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Jaipur International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":7.4,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Bais Godam railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":2.8,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Moti Dungri), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":18},{"id":"c00b08e7-4cb4-4c68-bfdd-b5e7799363fe","name":"Kheer Bhawani Temple (Ragnya Devi), Tulmulla","deity":"Kheer Bhawani (Ragnya Devi), worshipped over a heptagonal spring; the kuladevi of most Kashmiri Hindus","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Jammu and Kashmir","district":"Ganderbal","town":"Tulmulla","latitude":34.2211,"longitude":74.73,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Sind River","river_distance_km":3.3,"best_season_notes":"The Kheer Bhawani Mela on Jyeshtha Ashtami is one of the largest gatherings of Kashmiri Hindus after the Amarnath Yatra.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-26T21:24:56.957301+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Kalhana's Rajatarangini and the Bhrigu Samhita mention the site, and Abul Fazl's Ain-i-Akbari describes the marshy area. A legend says the yogi Krishna Pandit Taploo found the spring after a dream. Maharaja Ranbir Singh built a dharamshala; the present spring, pond and temple date from the 1910s under Maharaja Pratap Singh, and Hari Singh renovated it later. The legend was not independently verified.","etiquette_notes":"Devotees offer milk and kheer to the spring, and pilgrims sit or sleep on grass mats under the chinar trees.","native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":"Per commercial travel sources, not an official schedule: roughly 6am–8pm.","accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Srinagar Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":47,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Mazhom railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":16,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Kheer Bhawani Temple); Ganderbal district site","architecture_style":"Grey stone temple built over a spring","construction_century":20},{"id":"c0a5c68e-814b-4097-b36a-81895c11466a","name":"Pandori Dham","deity":"Vishnu as Bhagwan Narainji","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Punjab","district":"Gurdaspur","town":"Dinanagar Tahsil","latitude":32.0571,"longitude":75.5023,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Beas River","river_distance_km":5,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:44.755986+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Known formally as Thakurdwara Bhagwan Narainji, this historic temple in Pandori Mahantan village, Gurdaspur, belongs to the Ramanandi tradition. It is one of the fifty-two Vaishnava dvaras into which Bairagis are organised. Ramanandi saint Bhagwanji and his disciple Narainji founded it, and it is known for its Baisakhi fair.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Pathankot Air Force Station","nearest_airport_distance_km":23.3,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Gurdaspur railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":7.9,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Pandori Dham), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"c0a7f330-888b-42f7-a0ad-5981d118b4c4","name":"Tirunallar Dharbaranyeswarar Temple","deity":"Dharbaraneswarar (Shiva)","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":["Navagraha Sthalam"],"country":"India","state":"Puducherry","district":"Karaikal","town":"Thirunallar","latitude":10.92556,"longitude":79.79222,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Cauvery delta","river_distance_km":5,"best_season_notes":"Oct–Feb; especially crowded during Sani Peyarchi, Saturn's roughly 2.5-year sign transit.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-05T11:47:03.785954+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:00.624755+00:00","sthala_purana":"The best known of the Navagraha Sthalams, dedicated to easing the effects of Shani (Saturn). The site was once a forest of sacred dharba grass, and the original linga is said to have been formed of the grass itself — hence Dharbaraneswarar. Tradition holds King Nala, tormented by Shani's malefic influence, was freed of it after worshipping Shiva here, establishing the temple's enduring association with relief from Saturn's effects.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"தர்பாரண்யேஸ்வரர் கோயில், திருநள்ளாறு","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Thanjavur Air Force Station","nearest_airport_distance_km":77.8,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Karaikal railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":5.2,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Puranic/regional tradition (King Nala legend)","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"c0f45a77-88b9-4451-8777-76a545dd5cdd","name":"Nellaiappar Temple, Tirunelveli","deity":"Nellaiappar (Shiva) / Kanthimathi Amman","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":["Pancha Sabhai"],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Tirunelveli","town":"Tirunelveli","latitude":8.7139,"longitude":77.7567,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Thamirabarani","river_distance_km":0.5,"best_season_notes":"Nov–Feb.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-08T06:23:03.123234+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:00.624755+00:00","sthala_purana":"Historically two adjoining temples — one for Nellaiappar, one for his consort Kanthimathi Amman — later joined by the Sangili Mandapam (\"chain hall\"), added in the 18th century by the local merchant-patron Nainar Pillai and famous for its musical pillars, each carved to ring with a distinct note when struck. The temple houses the Tamira Sabha, the copper-roofed hall counted among the Pancha Sabhai, the five halls where Nataraja is traditionally held to have performed his cosmic dance.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"நெல்லையப்பர் கோயில்","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Tuticorin Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":29.8,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Palayankottai railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":2.2,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Local/regional tradition; Tamil Shaiva literature","architecture_style":"Dravidian, Pandya origins with later Nayak-era additions","construction_century":null},{"id":"c186a3c9-c7ba-4504-938f-fcc74a79b9d2","name":"M