t surviving examples of that architectural style in the Rayalaseema region, and today the official venue for Andhra Pradesh's state-sponsored Rama Navami wedding celebrations. Tradition holds Rama, Sita, and Lakshmana rested here during their forest exile, and that Rama shot an arrow into the earth to draw water for a thirsty Sita, forming the temple's two tanks, Ramatirtham and Lakshmanatirtham. The temple's own name is said to come from two devotees, Vontudu and Mittudu, credited with its construction.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"కోదండరామ ఆలయం, వొంటిమిట్ట","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Kadapa Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":33.9,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Mantapapalle railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":15.3,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Local/regional tradition","architecture_style":"Vijayanagara","construction_century":16},{"id":"c1fc36eb-65e6-42df-bfe4-4c473749acdf","name":"Radhakanta Temple, Chetla","deity":"Radhakanta (Krishna) with Radha and Lakshmi-Narayan","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"West Bengal","district":"Kolkata","town":"Kolkata","latitude":22.50612,"longitude":88.3398,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Adi Ganga","river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:03:52.882408+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:00.624755+00:00","sthala_purana":"A heritage temple in Chetla, Kolkata, built between 1796 and 1807 by Ramnath Mondal in the nine-pinnacled nabaratna Bengal style, rising nearly 100 feet beside the old Adi Ganga. It enshrines a black-stone Radhakanta with eight-metal images of Radha and Lakshmi-Narayan. It is said to have inspired the Dakshineswar Kali Temple.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Netaji Subhash Chandra Bose International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":19.9,"nearest_railway_station_name":"New Alipore railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":0.7,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Radhakanta Temple, Chetla), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Bengal nabaratna","construction_century":18},{"id":"c21e3ecc-ce2b-453b-a972-c472d1ab2d23","name":"Shri Swaminarayan Mandir, Tithal","deity":"Swaminarayan","sampradaya":null,"significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Gujarat","district":"Valsad","town":"Nanakvada","latitude":20.61194,"longitude":72.89139,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Wanki River","river_distance_km":0.2,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:03:52.882408+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A BAPS-run Swaminarayan temple right on Tithal beach in Valsad district, begun in 1991 and inaugurated by Pramukh Swami. Besides Swaminarayan, it has idols of Shiva and Parvati, Ganesha, Rama and Sita with Hanuman, and Krishna and Radha. Beach visitors often stop here, and its carved idols are admired.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"neares