ity":"Shiva as Kachabeswarar","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Chengalpattu","town":"Singaperumal Koil","latitude":12.77611,"longitude":79.99722,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Ninjalamadu River","river_distance_km":5.1,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:38.937899+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Shiva is worshipped here in lingam form, with Parvati as Antanatchi and Kanniyumaiyal. The Tevaram hymns praise the temple, which lies in a village of Kanchipuram district. Granite walls enclose the shrines, and the present masonry dates to the Nayak period, though Cholas are thought to have built the first complex.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Chennai International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":30.4,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Singaperumal Koil railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":1.6,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Kachabeswarar temple, Thirukachur), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Dravidian","construction_century":16},{"id":"c977b530-d3df-4b64-81a9-367d7fa5830b","name":"Purvesvara Siva Temple","deity":"Shiva as Purvesvara","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Odisha","district":"Khordha","town":"Bhubaneswar Municipal Corporation","latitude":20.23944,"longitude":85.84139,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Dayaa River","river_distance_km":3.1,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:03:52.882408+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A living 13th-century Shiva temple in Bhubaneswar's old town, about 300 m east of Lingaraja, which faces west. By local tradition the name reflects its position east of Lingaraja. A broken linga in a circular yonipitha sits in the sanctum, below ground level. Its hall is of the pidha type, and Sivaratri and Sankranti rituals are observed.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Biju Patnaik International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":3.3,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Bhubaneswar railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":3,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Purvesvara Siva Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Odisha (Kalinga)","construction_century":13},{"id":"c98d33ef-8513-43b6-9b9d-3d9dbc135d2c","name":"Siddheshwar Temple, Toka","deity":"Shiva as Siddheshwar","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Maharashtra","district":"Ahilyanagar","town":"Pravara Sangam","latitude":19.62228,"longitude":75.01408,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Godavari River","river_distance_km":0.2,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:59.639499+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A temple complex in Toka village described as a fine example of Yadava architecture of the 12th-13th centuries, with later additions from the Peshwa period. Its sculptures show scenes from the Ramayana, Mahabharata and Puranas, as well as celestial maidens and composite beasts. The sanctum has a large Shiva lingam with a brass snake and a Parvati image on the back wall.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Chhatrapati Sambhajinagar Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":48,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Nipani Vadgaon railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":32.6,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Siddheshwar Temple, Toka), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Yadava","construction_century":12},{"id":"c996d67d-7bde-4c34-8328-4e63b9872c38","name":"Ramanathaswamy Temple, Rameswaram","deity":"Shiva (Ramanathaswamy)","sampradaya":"Smartha","significance":["Jyotirlinga","Char Dham"],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Ramanathapuram","town":"Rameswaram","latitude":9.2882,"longitude":79.3129,"sandhya_friendly":"yes","sandhya_notes":"Agni Theertham beach directly behind the temple is the traditional spot for the 22 sacred well baths and Sandhya Vandanam.","samidhadhanam_friendly":"no","samidhadhanam_notes":"No dedicated firewood/samidha space known near the temple complex; most pilgrims skip this ritual here.","food_tier":"brahmin_run_kitchen","food_source_name":"Sri Vishnu Priya Bhavan","food_source_contact":"+91-4573-221-357","food_distance_km":0.4,"nearest_river_name":"Bay of Bengal (Agni Theertham)","river_distance_km":0.1,"best_season_notes":"Dec–Mar; this coastal island is directly exposed to the Bay of Bengal's northeast monsoon and occasional cyclones in Oct–Nov, on top of the extreme heat and humidity of the summer months.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-03T11:51:56.898831+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T11:30:32.947142+00:00","sthala_purana":"The Ramayana account relates that Rama, returning from Lanka, sought to expiate the killing of Ravana, a brahmin, by worshipping Shiva. Hanuman was sent to Kailasa for a lingam; when he was delayed, Sita fashioned one from sand. That lingam, the Ramalingam, is worshipped here, and Hanuman's Vishwalingam is honoured first by Rama's own instruction.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"இராமநாதசுவாமி கோயில்","morning_opens_at":"05:00:00","morning_closes_at":"13:00:00","evening_opens_at":"15:00:00","evening_closes_at":"20:00:00","timings_notes":"A coastal island temple; the 22 sacred wells (theerthams) inside have their own separate bathing routine, usually available throughout open hours.","accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Madurai Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":170,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Rameswaram Railway Station","nearest_railway_distance_km":2,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Shiva Purana / Skanda Purana (Jyotirlinga tradition)","architecture_style":"Dravidian","construction_century":13},{"id":"ca068d4c-5f03-4309-81af-60c95789fe7f","name":"Eklingji Temple, Kailashpuri","deity":"Eklingji (Shiva)","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Rajasthan","district":"Udaipur","town":"Kailashpuri","latitude":24.7167,"longitude":73.6931,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Ahar River","river_distance_km":6.5,"best_season_notes":"Oct–Mar. A complex of over a hundred shrines, not a single temple.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-03T20:39:31.59741+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"The tutelary deity (kuldevta) of the Mewar royal house, whose rulers traditionally styled themselves only as Eklingji's regents (Dewan). The four-faced marble Shiva image and the surrounding complex of shrines date back over a thousand years, though rebuilt several times.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"एकलिंगजी मन्दिर","morning_opens_at":"10:30:00","morning_closes_at":"13:30:00","evening_opens_at":"17:00:00","evening_closes_at":"19:30:00","timings_notes":"There is also an early Mangala darshan window, roughly 4:30–7am, not reflected in the two sessions above.","accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Maharana Pratap Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":23.6,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Ranapratap Nagar railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":15.3,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":null,"architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"ca9fe8ae-8308-4d7f-a645-50441c6ad3f7","name":"Badi Patan Devi Temple, Patna","deity":"Devi Sati, as a Shakti Peetha (the temple holds images of Mahakali, Mahalakshmi and Mahasaraswati, with Bhairav as guardian deity); a linked second shrine, Chhoti Patan Devi, stands about 4km away in Patna's Chowk area","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":["Shakti Peetha"],"country":"India","state":"Bihar","district":"Patna","town":"Patna","latitude":25.60531,"longitude":85.20629,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Ganges River","river_distance_km":1.3,"best_season_notes":"Durga Puja (Saptami–Navami) is the major festival, with reportedly around 1,000 daily visitors during it, and a Vijayadashami mela.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-22T09:21:41.744062+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Puranic Shakti Peetha tradition holds that Sati's right thigh fell here after Vishnu's Sudarshan Chakra cut her body — legend, not documented history. Patna's own name is popularly said to derive from \"Patan Devi,\" though that etymology is folk tradition rather than settled linguistics. Documented history is thinner: the current Badi Patan Devi structure is associated with the British-era figure Badrinath Chaudhary, while the linked Chhoti Patan Devi shrine (an ASI-listed monument) may date its rebuilding to the 16th–17th century, with some sources speculating an original core from the 9th–11th century — genuinely uncertain, and flagged as such by the sources themselves. Chhoti Patan Devi also holds older Brahmanical images (Ganesh, Vishnu, Surya) and architectural fragments, suggesting reuse of earlier material.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":"Per a third-party temple-info aggregator, not an official source: daily roughly 6am–10pm, with Tuesdays especially busy.","accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Jayprakash Narayan International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":12,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Patna Junction","nearest_railway_distance_km":10,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Puranic Shakti Peetha tradition; local/folk etymology; ASI listing (Chhoti Patan Devi)","architecture_style":"Small stone and brick shrine structures; black-stone deity images on raised simhasans","construction_century":null},{"id":"cb13215f-3be0-436a-8411-09dd80914744","name":"Singheshwar Sthan","deity":"Shiva as Singheshwar Mahadev","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Bihar","district":"Madhepura","town":"Singheswar","latitude":25.98365,"longitude":86.79552,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Koshi River","river_distance_km":1.3,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:59.639499+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Shiva temple in Madhepura, Bihar, important in the Mithila region and long a centre of tantric worship. Its legend is tied to the Ramayana, in which the sage Shringi performed a yajna for King Dasharatha. A month-long fair was held at Maha Shivaratri, and visitors also come in Shravan, Naga Panchami and Kartik Purnima.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Purnea Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":66.1,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Dauram Madhepura railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":8.4,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Singheshwar Sthan), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"cb773111-e3ad-4731-a773-3d0e407dc979","name":"Dobra Mahadev Temple","deity":"Shiva as Dobra Mahadev","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Rajasthan","district":"Bundi","town":"Balchand Para","latitude":25.46062,"longitude":75.63308,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Mej River","river_distance_km":10.3,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:38:36.086063+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Dobra Mahadev Temple is a Shiva temple in Bundi, Rajasthan. It holds cultural importance for the local community and draws thousands of visitors, according to the article.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Kota Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":39.6,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Bundi railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":6.1,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Dobra Mahadev Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"cc0e3cc5-6203-4ef3-8e48-496f4e3abee0","name":"Kapaleeshwarar Temple, Chennai","deity":"Kapaleeshwarar (Shiva) / Karpagambal","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":["Saptha Sthana Mylapore"],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Chennai","town":"Mylapore, Chennai","latitude":13.0338,"longitude":80.2695,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Adyar River","river_distance_km":2,"best_season_notes":"Feb–Mar for the Panguni Peruvizha (Arubathimoovar) festival; Oct–Feb otherwise.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-04T13:57:28.972216+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Originally built by the Pallavas in the 7th century near the present-day Santhome Church, destroyed during Portuguese colonisation in 1566, and rebuilt inland in its current form by the Vijayanagara rulers in the 16th century. Tradition holds Mylapore's name comes from Parvati worshipping Shiva here in the form of a peahen (mayil) after being cursed for losing focus during a Himalayan penance; a separate tradition holds Brahma installed a linga here after Shiva removed one of his five heads. Kapaleeshwarar is the seventh and largest of the Saptha Sthana Sthalangal, the seven Shiva shrines of Mylapore traditionally worshipped by the Saptarishis.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"கபாலீஸ்வரர் கோயில்","morning_opens_at":"05:00:00","morning_closes_at":"12:30:00","evening_opens_at":"16:00:00","evening_closes_at":"21:30:00","timings_notes":"Open 24 hours (5am to next-day 5am) on Maha Shivaratri.","accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Chennai International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":12,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Thirumayilai railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":0.3,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Local/regional tradition","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"cc195067-fee0-4f5f-8a78-507e4048f666","name":"Bhoga Nandeeshwara Temple, Nandi Hills","deity":"Bhoga Nandeeshwara (Shiva)","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Karnataka","district":"Chikkaballapur","town":"Nandi","latitude":13.37,"longitude":77.68,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Uttara Pinakini River","river_distance_km":10.5,"best_season_notes":"Oct–Feb.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-04T13:57:28.972216+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Among the oldest temples in Karnataka, with its earliest inscriptions dating to around 806 CE under the Nolamba and Rashtrakuta dynasties, and later additions by the Gangas, Cholas, Hoysalas, and Vijayanagara rulers across roughly a thousand years. The complex holds two adjoining shrines, Arunachaleswara and Bhoga Nandeeshwara, traditionally understood to represent Shiva's childhood and youth respectively, with a further Yoga Nandeeshwara shrine on the hilltop above representing his renunciation.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"ಭೋಗ ನಂದೀಶ್ವರ ದೇವಸ್ಥಾನ","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Kempegowda International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":19.4,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Chikballapur railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":8.5,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Local/regional tradition","architecture_style":"Ganga, Chola, Hoysala and Vijayanagara-era additions","construction_century":9},{"id":"cc2c02ca-091d-4547-92e9-5ee659a3efad","name":"Somnath Temple","deity":"Shiva (Somnath)","sampradaya":"Smartha","significance":["Jyotirlinga"],"country":"India","state":"Gujarat","district":"Gir Somnath","town":"Somnath","latitude":20.888,"longitude":70.4013,"sandhya_friendly":"yes","sandhya_notes":"The temple sits directly on the Arabian Sea shore; the beach area is used for sunrise Sandhya Vandanam.","samidhadhanam_friendly":"partial","samidhadhanam_notes":"Open ground near the parikrama path can work with your own samidha; nothing formally arranged.","food_tier":"pure_veg_available","food_source_name":"Somnath Trust pure-veg Bhojanalaya","food_source_contact":"+91-2876-231-212","food_distance_km":0.5,"nearest_river_name":"Arabian Sea (confluence of Hiran, Kapila, Saraswati rivers)","river_distance_km":0.1,"best_season_notes":"Oct–Mar; the sea breeze makes even midday pleasant in winter months.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-03T11:51:56.898831+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-04T08:49:12.455773+00:00","sthala_purana":"First among the Jyotirlingas. The sthala purana relates that Soma (Chandra), cursed by Daksha to waste away, worshipped Shiva at this shore and was released from the curse — recovering, then waning and waxing by turns, which is the origin of the lunar month. The temple has been destroyed and rebuilt many times over the centuries.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"सोमनाथ मन्दिर","morning_opens_at":"06:00:00","morning_closes_at":"13:00:00","evening_opens_at":"17:00:00","evening_closes_at":"20:00:00","timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Diu Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":85,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Somnath Railway Station","nearest_railway_distance_km":1,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Shiva Purana / Skanda Purana (Jyotirlinga tradition)","architecture_style":"Nagara","construction_century":11},{"id":"cc77ac7f-191c-4062-8cee-ee6200a61dd2","name":"Chamundeshwari Temple, Mysore","deity":"Chamundeshwari (Durga)","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":["Shakti Peetha"],"country":"India","state":"Karnataka","district":"Mysuru","town":"Mysuru","latitude":12.2724,"longitude":76.6702,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"pure_veg_available","food_source_name":"Dasoha Bhavana on Chamundi Hill Road — free breakfast, lunch and dinner daily","food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":0.3,"nearest_river_name":"Kabini River","river_distance_km":13,"best_season_notes":"Sep–Oct for Mysore Dasara, when the city and temple are at their most festive; Oct–Feb otherwise.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-04T13:20:34.20482+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Set atop Chamundi Hill above the city, reached by a flight of 1,008 stone steps past a monolithic Nandi carved from a single block of granite. Tradition holds this is where the goddess slew the buffalo-demon Mahishasura, giving the city of Mysuru (from Mahishasura's own city, Mahishuru) its name. The Wodeyar rulers of Mysore held Chamundeshwari as their family deity, and the temple was expanded considerably under their patronage.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"ಶ್ರೀ ಚಾಮುಂಡೇಶ್ವರಿ ದೇವಸ್ಥಾನ","morning_opens_at":"07:30:00","morning_closes_at":"14:00:00","evening_opens_at":"15:30:00","evening_closes_at":"21:00:00","timings_notes":"Overall hilltop gates open 6am–9pm. Abhishekam 6–7:30am and 6–7:30pm (5–6:30am on Fridays).","accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Mysore Mandakalli Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":5.1,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Ashokapuram railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":3.7,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Local/regional tradition","architecture_style":"Dravidian; the original shrine is Hoysala-era, with the towers rebuilt under later Vijayanagara and Mysore Wodeyar patronage","construction_century":17},{"id":"cc9bdba2-3d4c-4f22-abb2-0c58984a369d","name":"Girijatmaj Temple, Lenyadri","deity":"Girijatmaj (Ganesha)","sampradaya":"Ganapatya","significance":["Ashtavinayak"],"country":"India","state":"Maharashtra","district":"Pune","town":"Lenyadri (near Junnar)","latitude":19.2167,"longitude":73.8833,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Kukadi River","river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":"Ganesh Chaturthi (Aug–Sep) is the busiest day; Oct–Feb otherwise, and cooler for the roughly 300-step climb.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-04T13:05:55.016033+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-30T13:12:14.428399+00:00","sthala_purana":"Worshipped as Girijatmaj, \"son of Girija (Parvati)\" — Ganesha's child form. Local tradition holds Parvati did penance in this cave before Ganesha's birth. The shrine occupies Cave 7 of the ancient Lenyadri Buddhist cave complex, later adapted into a Ganesha shrine.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"श्री गिरिजात्मज मंदिर","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":"Sources disagree: one gives 6am–6pm with a Panchamrit Puja at 8am, another gives 5am–8pm. Neither source is authoritative; flagged, not resolved.","accessibility_notes":"A steep climb of roughly 300 stone steps up the hillside to Cave 7 (307 per one source, 338 per another); no wheelchair access is documented.","nearest_airport_name":"Pune International Airport (Lohegaon)","nearest_airport_distance_km":98,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Talegaon railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":85,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Lenyadri)","architecture_style":"A rock-cut Buddhist vihara of the 1st–3rd century CE, repurposed as a Hindu shrine rather than built in a classical temple style: an unpillared hall with 20 monk cells carved into the rock","construction_century":null},{"id":"cca1e712-01f0-4a94-859e-03da60f6a791","name":"Swaminarayan Akshardham (Gandhinagar)","deity":"Swaminarayan","sampradaya":null,"significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Gujarat","district":"Gandhinagar","town":"Gandhinagar","latitude":23.22917,"longitude":72.67417,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Sabarmati River","river_distance_km":1.3,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:03:52.882408+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A large BAPS Swaminarayan temple complex in Gandhinagar, built over 13 years under Pramukh Swami Maharaj as a tribute to Swaminarayan's life and teachings. The 23-acre site centres on a temple of about 6,000 metric tons of pink Rajasthan sandstone. The name refers to Swaminarayan's divine abode, where followers believe liberated souls go.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":17.6,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Gandhinagar Capital railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":4.5,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Swaminarayan Akshardham (Gandhinagar)), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"cccd8fa9-7b26-40b3-a0ae-f0a027cacd21","name":"Manyamkonda","deity":"Vishnu as Lakshmi Venkateshwara","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Telangana","district":"Mahabubnagar","town":"Kotakadra","latitude":16.64962,"longitude":77.88718,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Okacheti Vagu River","river_distance_km":9.8,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:38:01.041713+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A hill shrine of Lord Venkateshwara about 5 km from Devarakadra town, on the highway towards Raichur. It was the first temple in Telangana to offer ropeway access.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Rajiv Gandhi International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":86.9,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Manyamkonda railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":4.2,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Manyamkonda), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"cceeacc9-259b-4277-8bf5-f35f7030205f","name":"Dwarkadhish Temple, Mathura","deity":"Krishna as Dwarkadhish, with Radha","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Uttar Pradesh","district":"Mathura","town":"Mathura","latitude":27.50512,"longitude":77.68502,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":null,"river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:59.639499+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:00.624755+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Krishna temple in Mathura where he is worshipped as Dwarkanath or Dwarkadhish together with Radha. It follows the Pushtimarg tradition. The present building dates to 1814, raised by Seth Gokul Das Parikh, treasurer of Gwalior State, with support from Daulatrao Scindia.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Agra Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":46.8,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Shri Krishna Janam Asthan railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":1.4,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Dwarkadhish Temple, Mathura), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":19},{"id":"cd172782-8e2b-45f5-a0f9-0a9ca34be1ad","name":"Chausath Yogini Temple, Mitaoli","deity":"Shiva (with the sixty-four yoginis and Devi)","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Madhya Pradesh","district":"Morena","town":"Mitawali","latitude":26.43679,"longitude":78.23522,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Sank River","river_distance_km":7.7,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:47.875457+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"This eleventh-century temple in Morena district, Madhya Pradesh, was built during the Kachchhapaghata period and is among the better preserved Yogini temples in India. A circular wall holds 65 chambers, apparently for the 64 yoginis and Devi, around a central open pillared hall in the courtyard that is sacred to Shiva. It is also known as Ekattarso Mahadeva Temple.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Gwalior Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":15.5,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Malanpur railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":5.6,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Chausath Yogini Temple, Mitaoli), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Circular Yogini temple","construction_century":11},{"id":"cd9bde18-4400-44e1-8897-23c236705329","name":"Adi Kesava Perumal Temple, West Mambalam","deity":"Adi Kesava Perumal (Vishnu)","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Chennai","town":"West Mambalam","latitude":13.035,"longitude":80.2195,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Adyar River","river_distance_km":1.5,"best_season_notes":"Nov–Feb.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-08T06:51:40.218447+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Reported to be over 1,000 years old and, per local tradition, visited by the Sri Vaishnava acharya Ramanuja — distinct from the similarly named Adi Kesava Perumal temple in nearby Mylapore.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Chennai International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":7.3,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Mambalam railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":1,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Contributor-submitted local survey; local/regional tradition","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"cdcfa9fb-a8b8-43f1-aa84-d16e92f9bff2","name":"Amritaghateswarar-Abirami Temple","deity":"Shiva as Amritaghateswarar (Kalantaka) with Abirami","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Mayiladuthurai","town":"Thirumeiganam","latitude":11.0775,"longitude":79.81833,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Uppanar River","river_distance_km":4,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:53.924452+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Shiva temple at Thirukkadaiyur, Tamil Nadu, with Parvati as Abirami and a Vishnu shrine as well. It is linked to the legend of Shiva saving the young devotee Markandeya from death and to the saint Abirami Pattar. The 10-acre complex has an eleven-storey eastern tower and is praised in the Tevaram.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Neyveli Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":67.5,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Karaikal railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":18,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Amritaghateswarar-Abirami Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Dravidian","construction_century":9},{"id":"cde948a6-c5a0-4338-a33c-fb93cd38d453","name":"Palani Murugan Temple","deity":"Dhandayuthapani (Murugan)","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":["Arupadaiveedu"],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Dindigul","town":"Palani","latitude":10.45,"longitude":77.5167,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"pure_veg_available","food_source_name":"Temple Annadhanam scheme, running since 2002 — free meals 360 days a year","food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":0.2,"nearest_river_name":"Varadhamanadhi River","river_distance_km":2.2,"best_season_notes":"Jan–Feb for Thaipusam, one of the largest Murugan festivals anywhere — Palani's hill-station elevation keeps it noticeably cooler than the Tamil Nadu plains year-round, so it is a reasonable visit outside that window too.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-03T20:39:31.59741+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"One of the six Arupadaiveedu (sacred abodes of Murugan). Tradition holds Murugan retreated here alone, renouncing a mango offered as a prize to whichever of he and Ganesha could circle the world first, after Ganesha won by circling their parents instead. The image is said to be carved by the sage Bhogar from an amalgam of nine minerals (navapashanam).","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"பழனி முருகன் கோயில்","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Madurai Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":75,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Palani Railway Station","nearest_railway_distance_km":1,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":null,"architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"cdf597de-be37-4d14-a16c-940dc01f5e71","name":"Shiva Vishnu Temple, Poonga Nagar, Tiruvallur","deity":"Shiva and Vishnu","sampradaya":"Smartha","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Tiruvallur","town":"Poonga Nagar, Tiruvallur","latitude":13.147,"longitude":79.912,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Cooum River","river_distance_km":3.6,"best_season_notes":"Nov–Feb.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-08T06:51:40.218447+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A joint Shiva-Vishnu shrine in the Poonga Nagar residential locality of Tiruvallur town.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Chennai International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":32.5,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Tiruvallur railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":3.4,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Contributor-submitted local survey","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"cf340f95-606d-4f46-a820-a026da1dd08c","name":"Padmavathi Ammavari Temple, Tiruchanur","deity":"Padmavathi (Alamelu Manga), consort of Venkateswara","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Andhra Pradesh","district":"Tirupati","town":"Tiruchanur","latitude":13.60781,"longitude":79.45011,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Swarnamukhi River","river_distance_km":0.6,"best_season_notes":"The Karthika Brahmotsavam (about nine days) is the major festival, alongside Vasanthotsavam, Teppotsavam, Varalakshmi Vratam and Navaratri.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-26T20:40:38.920003+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Per one account, King Akasharaja found an infant girl in a golden lotus in a pond, named her Padmavathi, and she later married Srinivasa at Narayanavanam before residing at Tiruchanur. A related tradition holds that Lakshmi performed twelve years of penance in the temple tank and emerged from a golden lotus in the month of Karthika, which is why it is called Padma Sarovaram. These are two tellings of the origin rather than a contradiction, and both are tradition.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":"Wikipedia lists roughly 4:50am (3:30am on Fridays) to 9:30pm; this is not a confirmed TTD schedule, so check tirumala.org.","accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Tirupati Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":null,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Tiruchanur Railway